<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
  Copyright (c) 2026 Acmex Placeholder LLC

  Entitlements for the acmex binaries under the hardened runtime
  (docs/forge/CODE-SIGNING.md). Applied by `just sign-release` /
  `just resign-installed` when a Developer ID identity signs, and by
  release.yml's Developer ID step. The self-signed dev identity does
  not use the hardened runtime, so this file is inert for it.

  Empty by design: a plain command-line tool needs nothing here. Add
  ONLY what the program actually does, each with the reason:

  - com.apple.security.device.audio-input      opens the microphone
  - com.apple.security.device.camera           opens the camera
  - com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
        dlopens a dylib signed by ANOTHER team (an ONNX runtime, a
        vendor SDK); the notary service accepts it for Developer ID
  - com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
        JITs; almost never right for a Rust CLI

  A restricted entitlement (application-identifier, keychain-access-
  groups, Secure Enclave) is honored only inside an .app bundle with
  an embedded provisioning profile; a bare binary carrying one is
  killed at launch.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
